WEBVTT

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:09.440
Many students on our campus have been discussing whether university canteens should be open to the public.
校园里许多学生一直在讨论大学食堂是否应该向公众开放。

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:17.800
In my opinion, canteens should mainly serve students and staff, and they should be open to the public only on a limited basis.
在我看来，食堂应该主要为学生和教职员工服务，只在有限的范围内向公众开放。

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:22.360
The main reason is that canteens are already crowded at mealtimes.
主要原因是，食堂在用餐时间本来就很拥挤。

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:32.070
Students often have only a short break between classes, and if large numbers of visitors came in, lines would become longer and seats harder to find.
学生课间往往只有很短的休息时间，如果大量外来人员进入，排的队就会更长，座位也更难找。

00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:39.430
In addition, canteen meals are often subsidized by the university to keep prices low for students.
此外，为了让学生享受低价，食堂饭菜往往由学校提供补贴。

00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:45.910
Opening canteens fully to the public would strain these subsidies and might lead to higher prices.
食堂完全向公众开放会使这些补贴不堪重负，还可能导致价格上涨。

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:50.770
Food safety and campus security would also become harder to manage.
食品安全和校园安保也会变得更难管理。

00:00:51.570 --> 00:01:01.850
That said, canteens could welcome the public in a limited way, for example during off-peak hours or on weekends and holidays, when there are fewer students on campus.
话虽如此，食堂可以有限度地欢迎公众前来，例如在非高峰时段，或者在校园里学生较少的周末和节假日。

00:01:02.650 --> 00:01:05.840
Visitors could also be charged slightly more than students.
对外来人员的收费也可以比学生略高一些。

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:13.620
Such arrangements would allow canteens to share their services with the community without affecting students’ daily lives.
这样的安排能让食堂在不影响学生日常生活的情况下，与社区共享服务。
